## Issue Description
The issue describes a problem with multiple Processing Elements (PEs) connected to HBM memory. When several PEs connect to the same HBM, only one PE can correctly access its memory block because:

> "the adresses of the HBM blocks do not all start at 0. Instead all HBM blocks together form a continous address space"

Proposed Solution: TaPaSCo should automatically offset addresses for each PE to match the address range of its connected HBM block, ensuring each PE's address space starts at 0.

